+// Hegel properties for css-tree: the tokenizer against a second spec tokenizer, parse/generate as
+// a fixpoint, the lexer against values built from its own grammar, the walker, positions, clone
+// and plain-object conversion, List against an array, the name and value encoders against their
+// docs and the CSSOM idioms they cite, and the definition-syntax parser/generator round trip.
+// Each property draws one case record (see gen.mjs for the generators) and renders it with pure
+// functions; an operation list is applied with positions taken modulo the live size. The shapes
+// of the recorded bugs (bugs.toml) are drawn like any other and the properties fail on them,
+// naming the shape in the failure; each bug the wide properties do not shrink to also has a
+// property over its shape alone (the last section), and every bug has a pin (pins.mjs). HEGEL_NO_KNOWN=1 asks for a run that looks past the known bugs:
+// the generators then leave most of the shapes out, a mismatch that has one is skipped, and the
